  "worked_solution": "Note that the measure of the exterior angle at $D$ is ${180}^{∘}-(6x+{4}^{∘})={176}^{∘}-6x.$\n\nSince the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘},$  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9x-{17}^{∘})+(5x-{5}^{∘})+4x+({176}^{∘}-6x)+(3x+{11}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ (9x+5x+4x-6x+3x)+(-{17}^{∘}-{5}^{∘}+{176}^{∘}+{11}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 15x+{165}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 15x & ={195}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={13}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of the exterior angle of $∠A$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-{17}^{∘} & =9({13}^{∘})-{17}^{∘} \\\\  & ={117}^{∘}-{17}^{∘} \\\\  & ={100}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
